  metaDescription="Members leave when dues buy nothing they noticed. The five real reasons members quit, and a twelve-month renewal calendar that keeps them."
  h1="Why members leave associations, and the renewal calendar that keeps them."
  lede="Members rarely quit an association in anger. They quietly conclude the dues did not buy anything they noticed, and they let the renewal lapse. Retention is a twelve-month record of noticed value, and the renewal invoice is just the final exam."
  published="2026-09-21"
  heroImage={heroShot}
  heroAlt="Golfers loading silver carts staged on a path outside a clubhouse before an association outing."
  faqs={faqs}
  faqHeading="What boards ask us"
